  {
   "id": 535550,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/8accff1e971c6c9d.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n(credit: modification of work by Ziemer, Tim)\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>This graph shows the just noticeable difference versus the sound loudness. The CPS values show sound frequency.</p>\n<p>What is a claim that can be said based on this graph?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1048496,
     "content_html": "People cannot hear more minute differences for louder sounds."
    },
    {
     "id": 1048497,
     "content_html": "Sound frequency has no effect on hearing minute differences."
    },
    {
     "id": 1048498,
     "content_html": "People hear more minute differences in louder sounds."
    },
    {
     "id": 1048499,
     "content_html": "People can hear more minute differences in sounds with higher CPS (frequency)"
    }
